<h2 class="g-h2" id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>With a definition the pill gets <code>tabindex="0"</code> and a <code>.pill-tip</code> child. <code>assets/js/tooltips.js</code> positions that tip below the pill (above when there is no room), keeps it inside the viewport, and uses the Popover API where the browser has it so a clipping container cannot cut it off.</p>
  <p>The labels and their tiers come from <code>scripts/taxonomy.py</code>: change a tier there and every badge follows on the next build. <code>treatment_definitions</code> is written from the same file.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The tip is hidden with opacity rather than <code>display</code>, so a screen reader reads the label and then the definition; the tip's own copy of the label is <code>aria-hidden</code> so nothing is read twice. The definition opens on focus as well as hover. Never put an instruction only inside a tooltip.</p></div>

